hat they  need to offer a unified message with  simple core pillars that can be easily  distilled to win people over America is  freedom immigrants are bad poor people  are lazy corporations benefit everyone  these are simple ideas that anyone can  understand the left by contrast is prone  to infighting over all sorts of topics  some important but many frivolous who  cares how Nathan J Robinson dresses who  cares if chapo fans tweet snake emojis  at elected officials the closest the  left has come to offering a unified  platform is the push for Medicare for  all everyone in America should be able  to see a doctor without going bankrupt  that's easy to understand and it's an  idea just about everybody can get behind  regardless of political leaning these  core tenets shouldn't be hard to develop  it'll just take a little more  cooperation between podcasts tans  visibility on the other hand will be a  bit more difficult America has had at  least four decades of entrenched  right-wing media operations and they've  done an incredible job of shifting the  political conversation completely onto  the right side of the spectrum if the  left is to see any real success it must  develop platforms that can become  household names and offer a compelling  alternative to the  prevailing right-wing worldview the left  has the counterproductive habit of  deciding to start countless new  operations instead of backing the  already existing ones that could use the  support  why have thirty bad versions of the DSA  when the DSA already exists sure you  might not agree with them on every  single detail but it's the largest  socialist organization in the United  States and it'll have a lot more  influence than the United Greater North  Texas area a narco communist radical  Workers Party ever will that being said  the establishment of high-profile media  operations like means TV is a great move  now the left has its own streaming  service let's support them and spread  the word  make it a household name Hulu just kind  of existed for a while until suddenly  everybody was watching their content the  same can be true of means TV but only if  they have the funds to develop quality  original content the surge of  anti-capitalist films is a promising  sign too with one movie bong joon-ho is  able to catapult leftist talking points  onto the world stage take advantage of  that recommend it to your friends and  family talk about it afterwards help  grow the visibility of leftist ideas  while the left media landscape is still  comparatively small just look how much  it's grown in the past five years if you  had told me ten years ago that I would  have dozens of socialist podcasts and  YouTube channels to choose from thriving  leftist magazines to read and that  big-budget movies would explicitly  criticize the capitalist system all  within a decade I wouldn't have believed  you the resurgence of left media is real  it's modern its appealing and its timely  so anytime you're feeling down about the  state of the world remember that more  and more people are coming together to  try to change it and they need our  support if you enjoyed this video and  you'd like to see more like it consider  subscribing to stay up to date with my  latest episodes if you hated it go ahead  and drop a thumbs down and if you really  want to help support my channel I  recently started a patreon which you can  find at patreon.com slash second thought  you can check out my previous episodes  by clicking the links on your screen  thanks for watching and I'll see you  next week
 

